From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 01:30:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Bluetooth: btmtksdio: do not read the MT7668's command bitmap

The MT7668's supported-command bitmap claims LE Set Default PHY, which its
firmware rejects as unknown. The command is an HCI_INIT step, so the
failure aborts hci_init_sync() and the controller never reaches the
management layer: btmgmt lists no index.

Nothing lets a driver retract one claimed command, and
HCI_QUIRK_BROKEN_LE_CODED masks only the coded-PHY bit, so skip reading the
bitmap. The core then treats every optional command as absent; BR/EDR and
LE come up and discovery works.

Signed-off-by: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/bluetooth/btmtksdio.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/bluetooth/btmtksdio.c b/drivers/bluetooth/btmtksdio.c
index d2583bc..5ee35d1 100644
--- a/drivers/bluetooth/btmtksdio.c
+++ b/drivers/bluetooth/btmtksdio.c
@@ -1159,6 +1159,12 @@ static int btmtksdio_setup(struct hci_dev *hdev)
 		err = mt76xx_setup(hdev, bdev->data->fwname);
 		if (err < 0)
 			return err;
+		/* The MT7668's supported-command bitmap claims LE Set Default
+		 * PHY and its firmware answers Unknown HCI Command, which aborts
+		 * hci_init4. Skip reading the bitmap so the core never asks.
+		 */
+		if (bdev->data->chipid == 0x7668)
+			hci_set_quirk(hdev, HCI_QUIRK_BROKEN_LOCAL_COMMANDS);
 		break;
 	default:
 		return -ENODEV;
